      "read_view": "We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure\n [MATH S1.p1.m1: \\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x] on [MATH S1.p1.m2: \\mathbb{R}^{d}] , where\n [MATH S1.p1.m3: V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})] satisfies, for [MATH S1.p1.m4: 0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta] ,\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH S1.E1.m1: \\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,.] \n\n(1.1)\n\n\nThe main result of this paper is the following."
    },
