      "read_view": "Proposition 3.1 (Well-posedness and stationarity of the conditional phase space process).\n\n\n\nFor every fixed [MATH S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1: y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}] and initial phase space point\n [MATH S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2: (x_{0},p_{0})] , the event-driven dynamics in Algorithm 1, with\nthe reference point fixed at [MATH S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3: \\widetilde{x}] , defines a unique\nnon-explosive, time-homogeneous Markov process. The phase space measure\n [MATH S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4: \\nu_{\\eta,y}] is stationary for this process. In particular, the\nreturned position [MATH S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5: x_{\\pi}] is well-defined almost surely."
    },
