      "read_view": "Fix [MATH A1.SS1.p1.m1: y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}] . In the notation of\n(3.4), the bounce rate\n(3.9) reads\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex1.m1: \\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,[p^{\\top}h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)]_{+}\\,.] \n\n\n\nThe deterministic harmonic flow, namely the solution\n(4.5) of (3.8), and\nthe bounce map are\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex2.m1: \\displaystyle\\Phi_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)] \n [MATH A1.Ex2.m2: \\displaystyle\\coloneqq\\bigl(c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}+(x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\cos t+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p\\sin t,\\;-\\eta^{-1/2}(x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\sin t+p\\cos t\\bigr)\\,,] \n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex3.m1: \\displaystyle\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)] \n [MATH A1.Ex3.m2: \\displaystyle\\coloneqq(x,R_{h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)}p)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptR_{0}\\coloneqq I\\,.] \n\n\n\nThe bounce map is an involution. Although there is a possible discontinuity at [MATH A1.SS1.p1.m2: h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)=0] , this creates no ambiguity\nbecause the event rate vanishes there."
    },
