      ],
      "read_view": "To prove non-explosion, define the shifted harmonic energy\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex4.m1: H_{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl\\{\\eta^{-1}\\,\\|x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\|^{2}+\\|p\\|^{2}\\bigr\\}\\,.] \n\n\n\nThe flow and each bounce preserve this energy. Hence, with\n [MATH A1.SS1.p3.m1: \\mathcal{E}\\coloneqq H_{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x_{0},p_{0})] , every state produced by\nthe recursion satisfies\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex5.m1: \\|p\\|\\leq\\sqrt{2\\mathcal{E}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\|\\leq\\sqrt{2\\eta\\mathcal{E}}\\,.] \n\n\n\nBecause [MATH A1.SS1.p3.m2: \\nabla V] is [MATH A1.SS1.p3.m3: \\beta] -Lipschitz,\n [MATH A1.SS1.p3.m4: \\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\\leq\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})] throughout the path, where\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex6.m1: \\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})\\coloneqq\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\beta\\sqrt{2\\mathcal{E}}\\,\\bigl\\{\\sqrt{2\\eta\\mathcal{E}}+\\|c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}-\\widetilde{x}\\|\\bigr\\}\\,.] \n\n\n\nHence,\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex7.m1: \\int_{0}^{u}\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(\\Phi_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}}))\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\leq\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})\\,u\\,.] \n\n\n\nIf [MATH A1.SS1.p3.m5: \\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})=0] , the event rate\nvanishes and there are no jumps. Otherwise,\n(A.1) implies, for every finite waiting time,\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex8.m1: S_{n+1}\\geq\\frac{E_{n+1}}{\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})}\\,.] \n\n\n\nIf the recursion does not terminate, it follows that\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.Ex9.m1: T_{n}\\geq\\frac{\\sum_{j=1}^{n}E_{j}}{\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})}\\longrightarrow\\infty] \n\n\n\nalmost surely by the strong law of large numbers. Thus, the jump times\ncannot accumulate, and the recursive construction defines a unique\nprocess for all [MATH A1.SS1.p3.m6: t\\geq 0] . Finally, the\nmemoryless property of the exponential clocks gives the time-homogeneous\nMarkov property. This is precisely the integrated hazard construction\nof Davis [12, Section 2].\n∎"
    },
