      ],
      "read_view": "Proposition A.2 (Joint measurability and augmented space half-turn operator).\n\n\n\nThe family of conditional half-turn kernels\n [MATH A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1: (\\mathcal{H}_{y})_{y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}] admits a version, again denoted by\n [MATH A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2: \\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})] , such that\n [MATH A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3: (y,x)\\mapsto\\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,A)] is Borel measurable for every\nBorel set [MATH A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4: A\\subset\\mathbb{R}^{d}] . Consequently,\n\n\n\n\n\n [MATH A1.E9.m1: (\\mathsf{H}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x^{\\prime},y)\\,\\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})] \n\n(A.9)\n\n\ndefines a self-adjoint Markov contraction on [MATH A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5: L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta})] ."
    }
